# Line endings are part of the build contract on a mixed Windows/Linux
# project: CI runs on Linux, and the HarmonyOS toolchain (hvigor, the NDK's
# clang) is a Linux toolchain. A CRLF shebang script fails with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M", and a CRLF .nsh/.sh wrapper confuses hvigor.
#
# Keep everything that runs under a Unix shell as LF, keep Windows-only
# scripts as CRLF, and leave binaries untouched.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.ets text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.json5 text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jar binary
*.so binary
*.a binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
